  },
  "coverage": "32 London boroughs and the City of London; joined by official local authority code",
  "method_notes": [
    "Population change is derived from the start and end populations in the same ONS release, avoiding mixed revision vintages.",
    "Internal migration for a borough includes moves to and from other London boroughs as well as the rest of the UK.",
    "People and dwellings are different units. These comparisons do not estimate a housing shortage or convert migrants into households.",
    "Mid-year migration, financial-year delivery, October vacancy snapshots and calendar-year FDI have different reference periods; no causal relationship is estimated.",
    "HDT percentages are the published rounded results, not a newly calculated policy test.",
    "The City of London is retained in the data. Its small resident base should be considered when comparing rates.",
    "No borough investment or overseas-ownership observations have been inferred or fabricated."
  ],
